 # Working notes: b13d8adbb4ed
 
-Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
-Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+## 2026-10-24 direct repair
+
+The shape bank was only loosely “asymmetric”: four of nine shapes collapsed at least two of the five control operations after cropping. A bounded pre-fix probe found transform ambiguity in 121/300 generated examples, including S/zigzag shapes where identity equaled 180° and shapes where identity or CW equaled the horizontal flip. Those examples make the displayed control code locally unobservable.
+
+Generator v2.0.1 retains only five shapes whose normalized outputs are pairwise distinct under identity, CW, 180°, CCW, and horizontal flip. `self_check` now enforces that exact property. Diagnostic no-control/no-shape/symmetric textures are removed from the ordinary domain and rejected explicitly. A retained S-tetromino/code-3 hand case is still executed through the selected Racket rule: its canonical output equals the identity crop, and the repaired validator rejects it as transform-ambiguous.
+
+Verification: 1,536 deterministic draws over easy/medium/hard, all five control codes and all five retained shapes observed, six selected-rule protected-Racket labels, four focused regressions. Evidence is under `workspace/repair/evidence/`. Reviewer repair only; owner acceptance remains pending.
